       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I know you've confirmed it, but 2000 mg of sertraline daily is 10 times the maximum dose of 200 mg. You haven't given a clinical reason for it, and I can't see a scenario where scheduling it as a standing daily dose would be safe for this patient. The risks are serotonin syndrome, seizures, arrhythmia, and possible death.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter 50 mg, 100 mg, or 200 mg once daily, or any other dose up to 200 mg, as soon as you tell me which.\n- **Call pharmacy.** If you think there's an unusual indication, a clinical pharmacist or psychiatry can review it first. I can enter the order once the dose is verified.\n- **Call poison control.** If this is about an ingestion or overdose, it needs toxicology management, not a scheduled daily order. In the US, the number is 1-800-222-1222.\n\nLet me know how you'd like to proceed."
      }
     ],
